                <pb facs="0212" n="202" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv10/pg202"/>

                <head>Appendix 107</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Supreme Economic
                        Council for the Council of Ten</hi></p>
                <p>The attached memorandum has been approved by the Supreme Economic Council,
                    subject to approval by the Council of Ten of such questions as are not economic
                    in their nature and are, therefore, outside the scope of the Supreme Economic
                    Council.</p>
                <p>The memorandum is, therefore, submitted to the Council of Ten, and they are asked
                    in particular to give their approval to the following proposals:— <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>That an Inter-Allied Commission, consisting of four commissioners, one
                            from each Ally concerned with the administration of the occupied
                            territories, should, together with an Italian liaison officer, be set up
                            with full authority to co-ordinate the administration of the four Army
                            Commands on all economic, industrial and food questions, in accordance
                            with the policy laid down from time to time by the Supreme Economic
                            Council.</item>
                        <pb facs="0213" n="203" xml:id="pg203"/>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>That orders should be issued under the authority of the Supreme War
                            Council to the Army Commands in the various areas, that directions given
                            by the Commission shall be uniformly executed throughout the whole
                            area.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-04-15"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >April</hi> 15, 1919</date>.</dateline></closer>
